#    This preserves the original computation order while:
#      - improving instruction-level parallelism,
#      - exposing fixed-size inner loops that are easy for the C compiler
#        to auto-vectorize,
#      - maintaining good spatial locality for A, s, and p.
kernel_bicg_sched = divide_loop(
    kernel_bicg_sched,
    "j #1",              # the j-loop inside the i-loop
    J_TILE,
    ("jo", "ji"),
    tail="guard",
)
kernel_bicg_sched = unroll_loop(kernel_bicg_sched, "ji")

# 2) Apply the same tiling + unrolling pattern to the s-initialization loop.
